  "question": {
    "text": "For a statistical data $\\mathrm{x}_1, \\mathrm{x}_2, \\ldots, \\mathrm{x}_{10}$ of 10 values, a student obtained the mean as 5.5 and $\\sum_{i=1}^{10} x_i^2=371$. He later found that he had noted two values in the data incorrectly as 4 and 5 , instead of the correct values 6 and 8 , respectively. The variance of the corrected data is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$9$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$5$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$7$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$4$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { Mean } \\overline{\\mathrm{x}}=5.5 \\\\ & =\\sum_{\\mathrm{i}=1}^{10} \\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}=5.5 \\times 10=55 \\\\ & =\\sum_{\\mathrm{i}=1}^{10} \\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}^2=371 \\\\ & \\left(\\sum \\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}\\right)_{\\text {new }}=55-(4+5)+(6+8)=60 \\\\ & \\\\ & \\left(\\sum \\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}^2\\right)_{\\text {new }}=371-\\left(4^2+5^2\\right)+\\left(6^2+8^2\\right)=430\\end{aligned}$\r\n\r\n\r\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { Variance } \\sigma^2=\\frac{\\sum \\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}^2}{10}-\\left(\\frac{\\sum \\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{i}}}{10}\\right)^2 \\\\ & \\sigma^2=\\frac{430}{10}-\\left(\\frac{60}{10}\\right)^2 \\\\ & \\sigma^2=43-36 \\\\ & \\sigma^2=7\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}